# CODEOWNERS — the mechanism behind RULE-01 and RULE-09.
#
# Since ADR-004 unwired guard-registry.mjs, this file is what makes "the registry is human-only" true
# of a pull request. It moved the control from before the write to before the merge; it did not
# remove it. Deleting a line here removes a control, and nothing else will report that it is gone.
#
# TODO(project): replace @OWNER with the GitHub handle or team that must review these paths, and turn
# on branch protection requiring CODEOWNERS review. Until both are done, RULE-01 has no mechanism at
# all and the enforcement map in .ai/registry/rules.md is claiming something untrue.

/.ai/registry/    @OWNER
/.ai/standards/   @OWNER
/.claude/         @OWNER
/.github/         @OWNER
/.mcp.json        @OWNER

# TODO(project): add the schema or migrations directory once the datastore is chosen. Applying a
# migration is permanently human under RULE-09, and this is where that becomes true of a pull
# request rather than only of a sentence.
